pointers. It may not print custom object unless `operator<<`. But test uses `REQUIRE(data == tree->data())`, if fails, Catch2 prints `data` and `tree->data()`, both T. It may not print tree. `REQUIRE((bool) tree->left() == has_left)`, prints bool. 
